## Cheat Sheet

| Technique | Use it when | Time | Space |
| --------- | ----------- | ---- | ----- |
| Traversal | Counting, searching, printing | `O(n)` | `O(1)` |
| `prev` / `curr` pair | Deleting or inserting mid-list | `O(n)` | `O(1)` |
| Dummy node | Building a new list, or the head may change | `O(n)` | `O(1)` |
| Fast & slow | Finding the middle | `O(n)` | `O(1)` |
| Fast & slow | Detecting a cycle | `O(n)` | `O(1)` |
| In-place reverse | Need to traverse backwards | `O(n)` | `O(1)` |

**Pitfalls to check before you submit:**

- [ ] Handled the empty list (`head is None`) and single-node list?
- [ ] Handled deleting or replacing the **head**?
- [ ] Is the loop condition `while fast and fast.next` (not just `while fast`)?
- [ ] Saved `next_` **before** overwriting `current.next` when reversing?
- [ ] Does every loop actually advance its pointer on every path?

